        "**Hardening** reduces attack surface: remove unneeded software and services, close unused ports, change default credentials, apply least privilege, patch, enable host firewall and logging, and follow a baseline such as a CIS Benchmark or DISA STIG.",
        "**Normal Windows process tree**: `System` (PID 4) starts `smss.exe`; `wininit.exe` starts `services.exe` and `lsass.exe`; `services.exe` is the parent of `svchost.exe`; `winlogon.exe` launches `userinit.exe`, which starts `explorer.exe` and then exits.",
        "Red flags: more than one `lsass.exe`, `svchost.exe` whose parent is not `services.exe`, system binaries running outside `C:\\Windows\\System32`, misspellings like `svch0st.exe` or `scvhost.exe`, and Office apps spawning `cmd.exe` or `powershell.exe`.",
